[[2,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Proceed with removal \n                                          <a href=\"#/2429398\">5530B10</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Proceed with removal \n                                          <a href=\"#/2428998\">1048A32</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Proceed with the removal \n                                          <a href=\"#/2428915\">1048A10</a></p><p>Proceed with removal \n                                          <a href=\"#/2428924\">1056B60</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Proceed with removal \n                                          <a href=\"#/2428997\">1036L40</a>\n                                           .</p><p>1. Remove the camshaft protective plugs on the cylinder head extension.</p><p>2. Rotate the camshaft, using small movements, and fit the camshaft\ntiming tools.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>The camshaft timing adjustment\ntools are also used as leverage when unscrewing/tightening the rear\ngear retaining bolts.</p></aside><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>Locating pin</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.860.985.000</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2043954.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[4,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3>